Two reasons. First, spoilers sometimes ignore important factors. Some
lists even include monsters that do not, technically, leave corpses,
but would leave really cool corpses if they did. Second, you could
sacrifice them and improve your relationship with your divine patron
if your character did not count as a member of their race. Assuming
you're not an elf, you can sacrifice elves with impunity (regardless
of your alignment) even though they appear as @. Elven characters
likewise do not summon demons when they sacrifice nurses. The rules
for when a monster counts as a member of your race, now that I think
of it, change depending on context and basically require you to read
all available spoilers.


